Project Works means all activities to be carried out to complete the construction of the Project on the Project Area, including but not limited to:
- light maintenance roads;
- heavy maintenance roads;
- separate overhead crane to span the light maintenance roads;
- wheel lathe and bogie drop;
- graffiti cleaning road;
- heavy and light spares storage facility;
- through road, access roads and test road;
- sand silo;
- lay down and parking areas;
- ETCS / PSD interface testing facilities;
- offices, stores and staff facilities to support maintenance operations on the site;
- stabling facilities for twenty-six car train sets;
- facilities for train drivers and cleaners at the stabling facility;
- train wash;
- rail network connection;
- a construction camp, offices, temporary construction facilities; and
- ground excavation and vegetation clearing.

The Builder must:
(a) comply with all Environmental Applicable Requirements, and ensure the Builder Activities are carried out in a sustainable manner;
(b) take all reasonable and practicable measures to prevent or minimise harm to the Environment in the performance of the Builder Activities;
(c) subject to clause 24.6 (Contamination) and clause 24.6A (Disposal of PFAS Contaminated materials), promptly remedy any harm to the Environment arising out of or in connection with the performance of the Builder Activities;
(d) subject to clause 24.6 (Contamination) and clause 24.6A (Disposal of PFAS Contaminated materials), promptly remove from the Depot Site, the Ormeau Stabling Site and any other locations at which the Builder Activities are carried out or deal with, at the Builder’s cost, all waste, Contamination and debris resulting from, or arising out of or in connection with, performance of the Builder Activities, including removing or eliminating the cause of Contamination and any Contaminated material or substance;
(e) if an Environmental Incident occurs in connection with the Builder Activities:
(i) immediately report the Environmental Incident to the Contractor;
(ii) investigate the Environmental Incident;
(iii) advise the Contractor in writing of the outcome of the Builder’s investigation, including actions to be taken to remedy any damage to the Environment and prevent recurrence of the Environmental Incident; and
(iv) subject to clause 24.6 (Contamination) and clause 24.6A (Disposal of PFAS Contaminated Materials), at its cost, promptly take all reasonable steps to remedy any damage to the Environment (including clean up) and prevent recurrence of the Environmental Incident; and
(f) prepare, implement, maintain, update and comply with an Environmental Management System and the Environmental Management Plans (as applicable) in accordance with clause 14.1 (Preparation and implementation by the Contractor of Management Systems and Management Plans) and Schedule A5 (Management Systems (Builder) and Management Plans (Builder)).

