items.Requirement:
The Construction Environmental Management Plan - Ormeau Facility must describe how the Builder will ensure the delivery of Ormeau Facility Works meets environmental regulatory and policy requirements, and must address:
(a) how it will comply with the legislative and policy requirements including:
(i) any development conditions;
(ii) Commonwealth legislation;
(iii) State legislation;
(iv) Queensland Rail: Contractor Safety and Environment Management – MD-12-164; and
(v) Environmental Processes Manual (Transport and Main Roads, August 2013);

(b) the Builder’s approach to the management of environmental issues during the delivery of the Ormeau Facility Works including:
(i) environmental outcomes;
(ii) performance criteria;
(iii) mitigation measures;
(iv) monitoring;
(v) reporting; and
(vi) corrective actions;

(a) The Environmental Management System must:
(i) be consistent with AS/NZS ISO 14001:2004 Environmental Management Systems – Requirements with Guidance for Use and any subsequent Industry Standards;
(ii) demonstrate how environmental matters will be managed in a planned, systematic, effective and documented manner;
(iii) incorporate appropriate compliance, audit and verification processes;
(iv) provide for appropriate procedures and processes to identify, assess, control and minimise environmental risks arising from the Builder Activities; and
(v) provide for monitoring and reporting of environmental performance, including compliance, to drive continual improvement.

The EMP – Ormeau Facility must address all aspects of the design and construction of the Ormeau Facility and must:
(a) be consistent with the Builder’s Environmental Management System;
(b) address how the Builder will ensure compliance with Environmental Applicable Requirements and the Environmental Management System in the performance of the Builder Activities;
(c) identify employees and officers responsible for management of Environmental issues;
(d) describe relevant training processes implemented by the Builder and its Subcontractors to ensure compliance with Environmental Applicable Requirements and the Environmental Management System;
(e) describe the Builder’s systems for monitoring and reporting on Environmental Incidents and potential Environmental Incidents; and
(f) describe how the Builder will manage and maintain records and information relating to compliance with Environmental Applicable Requirements in the performance of the Builder Activities.

