4.3.10 The design and construction of the Ormeau Facility must:
(a) not increase afflux by more than 10mm at any neighbouring habitable property for a 1% AEP event; (Note: The area depicted in Figure 28-1: Non-habitable property in Civil and Drainage section 3 (d) in 5.2.2 – Ormeau Facility Site Layout Proposal of Schedule C3 ((Contractor Proposal (Ormeau Facility)) of the Project Deed was not considered to be habitable property in the development of the design of the Ormeau Facility. The State will work with the Contractor and the City of Gold Coast City Council as required on this matter)
(b) not reduce the flood immunity or increase the flood hazard associated with any public road, rail or pedestrian asset;
(c) consider risks posed to neighbouring properties and emergency access/egress for events larger than the 1% AEP event to minimise unexpected or unacceptable impacts;
(d) consider all floodplain impacts outside of the Ormeau Facility including changing in peak velocity, time of inundation, flood flow distribution, and flood hazard to minimise unexpected or unacceptable impacts; and
(e) not worsen the existing flooding characteristics of the Woongoolba Flood Mitigation Scheme.
(Note: The flood data provided by City of Gold Coast Council including, but not limited to:
(i) Woongoolba_URBS_v2016_2100_MFlood;
(ii) Woongoolba MIKE Flood v2016c;
(iii) Draft PimpSandy_URBS_v2.1.5;
(iv) Draft LoganAlbert_URBS_v2.1.5;
(v) Draft Logan_AlbertTUFLOW_v2.3.5a_2020; and
(vi) Draft Logan_AlbertTUFLOW_v2.3.6a_2100.)

4.11.2 The Contractor must:
(a) provide, maintain and service, decommission and rehabilitate all temporary site facilities including offices, amenities and crib facilities at the Ormeau Facility Site required to deliver the Ormeau Facility Works;
(b) undertake and provide any mobilisation activities, temporary works and site establishment works to allow for the safe and efficient operation of the Ormeau Facility Works;
(c) secure the Ormeau Facility Site through necessary means to prevent unintended public access;
(d) install and maintain the temporary fencing and hoardings on the Ormeau Facility Site boundaries, road boundaries and at other locations as necessary to provide for safety and security in the performance of the Ormeau Facility Works and to prevent motorist distraction. The fences and hoardings must be erected prior to work commencing in the affected areas;
(e) construct any necessary temporary laydown, vehicle parking and equipment storage areas to support the Ormeau Facility Works;
(f) provide secure storage for safety equipment, construction, maintenance and repair plant and material as required to fulfil the obligations of the Project Deed, this specification, and the Technical Requirements;
(g) establish any on-site maintenance facilities and workshops as required to service and support the construction plant and equipment, including any fuel or oil storage compounds;
(h) maintain the Ormeau Facility Site and any other construction site in a clean and tidy manner throughout the Ormeau Facility Works. The extended storage of rubbish or loose items on the Ormeau Facility Works or elsewhere is not permitted; and
(i) locate site sheds at locations and positions that minimise the impact on Adjoining Land to the Ormeau Facility Site.

